> **DISABLED — DO NOT RUN HEADLESSLY.** Feeding this file to `claude -p` starts a
> scheduler that believes it owns the ledger. Doing that in a loop is what caused the
> 38-generation duplicate-director storm on 2026-07-25 (see ADR-0012). The only
> sanctioned launch is a single interactive `claude --agent dream-director`, started and
> rotated by hand. There is no supervisor and no automated relauncher.

# Resume prompt — dream program director

Any fresh session resuming this program: paste the full Program Director operating
prompt (the one containing PART 0–10 and START HERE). `.program/ledger/items/ROOT.md`
exists, so START HERE routes you to PART 10 automatically.

Facts a successor should not re-derive:
- Genesis completed 2026-07-25 (director-gen0). Levels: Program → Phase → Capability /
  Contract → Feature / Task / Probe / Gate (see glossary.md).
- Phases ROOT.1..ROOT.5 are strictly ordered; ROOT.6 (Hosted) is PARKED (ADR-0001).
- ROOT.2.4 (legacy progress cutover/archival) is PARKED — dual-write is the end-state
  until the owner authorizes.
- Settled at genesis, do not silently revisit: ADR-0001..0006 in .program/decisions/.
- Roles: 21 dream-* files; .program/roles/ is authoritative, user-scope
  C:\Users\jainv\.claude\agents\ is the loaded copy — regenerate user-scope from the
  mirror on drift, never the reverse.
- The director alone runs git, on the program repo, on a timer.
- Port 3000 is the owner's. Never AskUserQuestion. Debugging is always fanned out.
